<Sequence DisplayName="Strategy A - DOUBLE_BOOKING" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_9">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Who keeps the time is rule-based, never arbitrary:
  priority (URGENT, HIGH, NORMAL) -&gt; follow-up first -&gt; earliest created -&gt; lowest id

For each loser, ESCALATE instead of moving when:
  inside min_reschedule_notice_hours (4h)       TOO_CLOSE_TO_RESCHEDULE
  follow-up with a previous appointment         TREATMENT_CYCLE_NEEDS_APPROVAL
  priority URGENT                               URGENT_NEVER_AUTO_MOVED
  already moved max_reschedules_per_appointment AMBIGUOUS_PRIORITY
  no viable slot within reschedule_window_days  NO_REPLACEMENT_SLOT

FindReplacementSlot reuses SchedulingBot's AllocateSlot.xaml, so a moved
patient is treated by exactly the same fairness rules as a new one.
The HMS enforces these rails too and returns the same codes from
/admin/reschedule — the bot checks first so it can escalate with a SuggestedSlot.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
